{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py` re-exports 7 names it does not define, each marked\n`# noqa: F401  (re-exported for back-compat)` — 3 from `._processors_identity`\n(`_rederive_keyring_keys`, `process_key_event`, `process_signature`) and 4 from\n`._processors_status` (`_fold_claimed_session`, `_fold_close_metadata`,\n`_fold_plan_review_phase`, `process_status`). ADR 0111 forbids internal shims.\n\nCensused on `origin/main` at `50d5a36539d` by parsing every `.py` under `src`, `tests`\nand `scripts` with `ast`, resolving relative imports, and separately scanning\n`ast.Attribute` and string constants:\n\n- **4 names have zero importers** and can be deleted outright: `_fold_claimed_session`,\n  `_fold_close_metadata`, `_fold_plan_review_phase`, `_rederive_keyring_keys`. None is\n  used inside `_processors.py` either, so they are dead in both directions.\n- `process_key_event` — 1 importer, production: `src/rebar/reducer/_replay.py:19`.\n- `process_signature` — 5 sites: `_replay.py:19` plus\n  `tests/unit/test_attestations_reducer.py:13`,\n  `tests/unit/test_legacy_signature_mirror_drop.py:15`, and `tests/unit/test_signing.py`\n  at both `:117` and `:133`.\n- `process_status` — 6 sites: `_replay.py:19` plus\n  `tests/unit/test_attestations_reducer.py:13`, `tests/unit/test_claimed_session.py:20`,\n  `tests/unit/test_harness_provenance.py:20`,\n  `tests/unit/test_plan_review_phase_happy.py:6`, and\n  `tests/unit/test_plan_review_phase_reducer.py:10`.\n- No attribute-style access (`_processors.process_status(...)`) anywhere.\n- Two string constants contain `rebar.reducer._processors`; both were read and neither\n  needs editing. See Out of scope.\n\nA line-oriented grep for `from rebar.reducer._processors import <name>` reports 0\nimporters for `process_key_event` and misses `test_attestations_reducer.py` entirely,\nbecause `_replay.py` and that test import inside multi-line parenthesized statements\nwhere the name sits on its own line. The AST census above is the correct instrument;\nthe grep count is not.\n\n## Change\n\n1. Repoint the 3 names that have importers to the modules that define them:\n   `process_key_event` and `process_signature` to `rebar.reducer._processors_identity`,\n   `process_status` to `rebar.reducer._processors_status`.\n2. **Four** importers pull a genuine `_processors` member on the same statement, so they\n   must be split rather than rewritten wholesale:\n   - `src/rebar/reducer/_replay.py:19` imports 18 names, of which 3 move — and they come\n     from two different siblings, so this becomes **three** statements: 15 names stay on\n     `_processors`, `process_key_event` and `process_signature` go to\n     `_processors_identity`, `process_status` to `_processors_status`.\n   - `tests/unit/test_attestations_reducer.py:13` imports `attestation_kind`,\n     `process_signature`, `process_snapshot`, `process_status` — likewise **three**\n     statements: `attestation_kind` and `process_snapshot` stay, `process_signature`\n     moves to `_processors_identity`, `process_status` to `_processors_status`.\n   - `tests/unit/test_legacy_signature_mirror_drop.py:15` and\n     `tests/unit/test_plan_review_phase_reducer.py:10` each also import\n     `process_snapshot`, defined in `_processors.py` at `:469`, which stays — two\n     statements each.\n3. Delete all 7 re-exports from `_processors.py`. The whole\n   `from ._processors_status import (...)` statement goes, since all 4 of its names are\n   re-export-only. The `._processors_identity` statement keeps\n   `_bootstrap_genesis_keyring` (used at `:139`, `:520`), `_fold_author_attribution`\n   (`:81`, `:185`, `:296`) and `attestation_kind` (`:508`), which carry no `noqa`\n   because `_processors.py` uses them.\n4. Extend the held-out oracle `tests/unit/test_internal_shims_removed_3a46.py`, which\n   already covers `_processors`/`_processors_status` and sets the convention: assert the\n   re-exports are absent AND that the canonical modules still expose them, so the\n   assertion cannot pass vacuously.\n5. Add a `docs/release-notes.md` entry naming the 3 import paths that moved\n   (`process_key_event`, `process_signature`, `process_status` are no longer importable\n   from `rebar.reducer._processors`) and the module that now owns each.\n\n## Testing\n\n- A case in `tests/unit/test_internal_shims_removed_3a46.py` asserting\n  `not hasattr(_processors, name)` for all 7 names, paired with positive assertions that\n  `_processors_identity` and `_processors_status` still expose them.\n- The repointed test modules must stay green unchanged in substance — only their import\n  lines move.\n- `make verify` covers the whole-tree effect, including the reducer replay suites that\n  exercise `_replay.py`'s dispatch, which is the one production consumer.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] **AC1** `grep -cF 're-exported for back-compat' src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py`\n      prints 0.\n- [ ] **AC2** Re-running the AST census reports 0 importers for all 7 names.\n- [ ] **AC3** `python -c \"from rebar.reducer import _processors as p; assert not any(hasattr(p, n) for n in ['_rederive_keyring_keys','process_key_event','process_signature','_fold_claimed_session','_fold_close_metadata','_fold_plan_review_phase','process_status'])\"`\n      exits 0.\n- [ ] **AC4** `python -c \"from rebar.reducer._processors_identity import process_key_event, process_signature; from rebar.reducer._processors_status import process_status\"`\n      exits 0, proving the moved names stay reachable at their canonical modules.\n- [ ] **AC5** `python -c \"from rebar.reducer._processors import process_snapshot, attestation_kind\"`\n      exits 0, proving the two names that stay on `_processors` are unaffected.\n- [ ] **AC6** `ruff check src tests` exits 0 with no output.\n- [ ] **AC7** `pytest tests/unit/test_internal_shims_removed_3a46.py -q` exits 0.\n- [ ] **AC8** That file's collected case count is strictly greater than its count on\n      `origin/main`, measured with `pytest --collect-only -q` on both.\n- [ ] **AC9** `git diff --name-only origin/main...HEAD` lists exactly 11 paths:\n      `src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py`, `src/rebar/reducer/_replay.py`, the 7 named\n      test modules, `tests/unit/test_internal_shims_removed_3a46.py`, and\n      `docs/release-notes.md`.\n- [ ] **AC10** `docs/release-notes.md` gains an entry naming all 3 moved import paths,\n      and the file's only diff is additions.\n- [ ] **AC11** `make verify` exits 0.\n\n## Ordering\n\nIndependent of the resolver-shim story `insanitary-divine-moa` — different modules, no\nshared source file. Either may land first.\n\n## Out of scope — checked, not merely unexamined\n\n- `attestation_kind`, which 5 files import from `_processors`\n  (`src/rebar/_commands/verify_opcert.py:45`, `src/rebar/_opcert_signing.py:354` and\n  `:437`, `src/rebar/_opcert_verify.py:176`, `tests/unit/test_attestations_reducer.py:13`).\n  It is **not** a re-export: `_processors.py` uses it itself at `:508`, so its import\n  stays and carries no `noqa`. Repointing those 5 importers is a separate judgement call,\n  not part of removing re-exports.\n- `tests/unit/test_plan_review_phase_reducer.py:63`, which captures logs on the logger\n  named `\"rebar.reducer._processors\"`. That record is emitted at `_processors.py:495`\n  inside `process_snapshot`, under that module's own `logging.getLogger(__name__)`, and\n  `process_snapshot` stays — so the string remains correct and must not be changed.\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/_field_contract.py:114`, whose `notes=` prose names\n  `rebar.reducer._processors.process_tag_delta`. That function is defined in\n  `_processors.py` at `:434` and stays, so the prose stays accurate.\n- The `_engine_support/resolver.py` shim, tracked on `insanitary-divine-moa`.\n- Any behavior change in the processors themselves."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793379296627665324,"uuid":"11304576-c196-4a4b-a550-baaa8e027247"}